\buffersize sets the size of the audio buffer used by
Python (pyo), in samples. The default is 256.
It takes one argument, an integer:

\buffersize 512

The audio settings are applied only once, when \python is
called for the first time. For this reason, this command
must be called before \python, otherwise it has no
effect. It also has no effect if LiveLily is built
without pyo.

See also \samplerate, \inchannels, \outchannels and
\setaudiodev.
